#
# compose/env/local.env.example — operator-tunable variables consumed by
# compose/docker-compose.local.yml (T015, local profile).
#
# Copy to compose/env/local.env (gitignored) and edit. The default values
# below are what `scripts/stargate init` (T016) will write for the local
# profile; for the bring-your-own-env path, copy this file and override.
#
# The local profile is opinionated: the loopback-only DP port (8881), the
# Tor SocksPort/ControlPort (compose-internal only), the UID/GID numerics
# (stargate-cp 5101, stargate-dp 5102, stargate-ipc GID 5100), and the
# named-volume set are NOT operator-tunable — they are the contract the
# rest of the system (T019b/T022 contract tests, the rendered torrc, the
# inter-plane UDS topology) is wired against.
#
# T094a removed the docker-socket-proxy auxiliary container and with it
# the only external image this profile previously pulled
# (tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy). The three remaining services are all
# Stargate-built via `build:` directives whose content pin is the
# base-image digest encoded in each Dockerfile (data-plane/Dockerfile,
# control-plane/Dockerfile, sidecars/tor/Dockerfile); final-image digest
# pinning for those is a release-tag-time concern (T081). This file
# therefore declares NO operator-tunable image variables for the local
# profile today; it is retained as the env-file shape `docker compose
# --env-file` consumes and as the home for any future operator knob.
